Actually this is simpler than I thought. For every non-bg pixel outside the seed, it places a copy of the entire seed pattern such that the seed pixel at position (sr, sc) relative to the seed center gets placed at (r, c). So the seed gets repositioned so its center aligns with the current non-seed pixel at (r, c).

